 ],
 "text": "Uber is giving AI to all 30,000 staff. The secret wasn't the tool. It was 30 experts sitting next to teams for 2 weeks. Here's what happened. They started with a pilot of about 1,000 people. 8 in 10 of them weren't engineers. Then 30 AI engineers sat with each team, found the boring parts of their jobs and automated them. Data reports. Training in new languages. Dashboards. 2 weeks per team. Then they scaled. Most companies do the opposite. They buy licenses for everyone, send a login, and wonder why nobody uses it. You don't need 30 engineers. You need someone next to your team for 2 weeks. On your real work. Bring your biggest bottleneck to our free office hours. Link in bio."
